Hi A,&nbsp;The responses is needed to MBs email Friday, October 17, 2025 1:22 pm (it’s on the Pallas ‘Report’ email string). &nbsp; Updated wording below.&nbsp;&nbsp;----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&nbsp;Dear Michael, Priyanka, and Sarah, &nbsp;I refer to your below email of 17 October 2025 addressed to the Board which you state is intended to be a protected disclosure.&nbsp;The Firm takes any professional and regulatory concerns raised by anyone at the Firm very seriously and so I firstly want to thank you for raising your concerns with the Board. &nbsp;As COLP, I will be investigating your concerns in accordance with our Whistleblowing Policy. Please be aware that based on my current knowledge, my initial views are that the allegations are unfounded, nevertheless I expect to provide you with a fuller response in relation to the content of your below email once this investigation has been completed – which I will do by the end of this week.&nbsp;&nbsp;Should you have any questions or further concerns in the meantime, please do not hesitate to reach out to me. &nbsp;Kind regardsAlicia&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Helena&nbsp;YearwoodRisk&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Compliance&nbsp;DirectorFrom: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 21 October 2025 16:13To: Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Fw: Bond turner/Pete/Anna&nbsp;Is this the email I'm responding to as COLP? I've lost the thread on which one.&nbsp;​​​​Alicia&nbsp;AliniaChief&nbsp;Executive&nbsp;Officer+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;629From: Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: Tuesday, October 21, 2025 12:30 PMTo: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Bond turner/Pete/Anna &nbsp;Hi both,&nbsp;Just following up on this please. Can you let me know the &quot;why&quot; when you have a moment?&nbsp;Thanks,Michael​​​​Michael&nbsp;Burke(He/Him)Partner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7960&nbsp;032&nbsp;34407960&nbsp;032&nbsp;344From: Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: 15 October 2025 3:34 PMTo: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Bond turner/Pete/Anna &nbsp;Hi Alicia,&nbsp;&nbsp;Understood thanks. An explanation on why would be helpful and (I'm sorry to say) necessary so I can consider when advising the clients.&nbsp;&nbsp;Agreed - each of the silks did a great job, especially Ben Jaffey (with my Ford hat on). They don't quite have the same pizzaz as ours did do they!&nbsp;&nbsp;Thanks,&nbsp;Michael&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Michael&nbsp;Burke(He/Him)Partner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7960&nbsp;032&nbsp;34407960&nbsp;032&nbsp;344From:&nbsp;Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Wednesday, October 15, 2025 2:29 PMTo:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: Bond turner/Pete/Anna &nbsp;Thanks Mike. Yours and the rest of the co-leads comments and suggestions are duly noted.&nbsp;&nbsp;For completeness, I agree with Anna.&nbsp;&nbsp;Btw, Tom D M got us off on an amazing start! Perhaps my bias but I can't say the same thing about the defendants' openings.&nbsp;&nbsp;Kind regards,A&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Alicia&nbsp;AliniaChief&nbsp;Executive&nbsp;Officer+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;629From:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Wednesday, October 15, 2025 2:12 PMTo:&nbsp;Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: Bond turner/Pete/Anna&nbsp;Hi Anna, Alicia,&nbsp;Thanks for bringing Alicia in - it's important we all consider this and the implications. It would also (at least to me) make sense to bring in the PG Case Leads, but I will leave that to you.&nbsp;&nbsp;The SteerCo is only applicable to the Mercedes GLO, not to Ford, PCD and Renault Nissan - all cases which we are co-lead solicitors with LD and there is no SteerCo. If LD and the PG Case Leads think Pete should be involved - then plainly he should be. The Case Leads on those cases should be unencumbered to instruct him if they believe it is in the best interests of their clients - which we do.&nbsp;The advice of the co-Lead Solicitor, all of the Case Leads and all of those who have been involved in the cases for years (indeed for me - it has been half a decade) should make the decision obvious. Instructions in opposition to the clear advice need to have firm grounding and I am afraid that I can't see that the below do. I am afraid I don't understand why you don't want to involve Pete or why you don't think it is the best interest of the clients. Can you explain that?&nbsp; And explain why it is in their best interests to shut out one of the main architects of the Pan NOx Litigations who has a huge level of knowledge to input?&nbsp;I agree it we need to focus on the trial, and this is precisely what involving Pete will assist with - allowing me and the other case leads to focus on the trial while Pete assists on quantum.&nbsp;&nbsp;I also note you have said you are in the process of reading in. If I recall correctly, you also said that your primary role (or one of them) would be dealing with all of the firm specific issues that would be arising e.g. FID, SFC and champerty, over the coming months. Given the indications of the Defendants at the last PM, alongside the other issues the firm is facing, I imagine this will require significant time such that it would be to the quantum workstreams loss if you tried to manage PDD, Quantum and that workstream. Decisions are needed now and cannot wait.&nbsp;I don't believe we need to speak to Martyn about this to reach a landing do we - we have all made our feelings very clear that it is in the best interests of the clients. If we are prevented from doing so then it is preventing us from doing what we, as the appropriate solicitors with conduct of the cases, view as acting in the best interests of our clients.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Thanks,Michael&nbsp;​​​​Michael&nbsp;Burke(He/Him)Partner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7960&nbsp;032&nbsp;34407960&nbsp;032&nbsp;344From:&nbsp;Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Wednesday, October 15, 2025 11:00 AMTo:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: Bond turner/Pete/Anna&nbsp;Hi Michael,&nbsp;Thanks for your email. I have copied Alicia.&nbsp;&nbsp;I have indeed seen Priyanka's email but not had a chance to respond yet. I know that you state it is in the claimants' interest but I do not think it is necessarily so. Indeed, this has been discussed with the Steering Committee and it was agreed as a group and per the GLO that it is not the right time (that includes Hausfeld, Milberg, S&amp;G and Leigh Day also agreed with it at the time). Moreover, Bond Turner had expressed a view but not the CSG as a general. The point is being actively considered and that is why we are engaged in discussions.&nbsp;&nbsp;We are both in court today. I suggest we focus on that for today and we try and collaborate despite your strong views on the matter.&nbsp;&nbsp;BestAnna&nbsp;Sent from Outlook for iOS​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Wednesday, October 15, 2025 10:48 amTo:&nbsp;Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: Bond turner/Pete/Anna&nbsp;Hi Anna,&nbsp;Removing the others from this chain.&nbsp;&nbsp;You'll have already seen the email chain from the case leads (sent by Priyanka) on this matter. I attach it for ease.&nbsp;&nbsp;We, as case leads, firmly believe it is in everyone's (most of all the clients) best interests for Pete to be brought in to advise on PDD and Quantum, and that if he is shut out, this is actively acting in a prejudicial manner to our clients and the clients of the other claimant law firms. It would be ignoring the strong advice and wishes of everyone - co-joint Lead Solicitors, non-lead Claimant Firms, PG Case Leads and Counsel, if Pete is not involved.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;That you have said the trial is in October next year highlights a fundamental underappreciation of the complexity and nature of these proceedings. Decisions made now have a direct bearing and determination on the Trial next year. That the trial is in October next year is a red herring.&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;He should be involved and involved from now, rather than waiting to discuss, as the longer he is kept out the more issues present.&nbsp;Thanks,&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Michael&nbsp;Burke(He/Him)Partner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7960&nbsp;032&nbsp;34407960&nbsp;032&nbsp;344From:&nbsp;Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Wednesday, October 15, 2025 10:22 AMTo:&nbsp;Martyn Day &lt;mday@leighday.co.uk&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Nichola Marshall &lt;nmarshall@leighday.co.uk&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Sapna Malik &lt;smalik@leighday.co.uk&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: Bond turner/Pete/Anna&nbsp;Morning Martyn, all&nbsp;Happy to meet and discuss. However, could we meet either before or after 12 on Friday - I already have a call then.&nbsp;&nbsp;In terms of Quantum, the trial is listed for October next year. We have a new legal director joining Monday and another should be able to join shortly after that. I am also reading in now. We have a further 2 further associates who are keen to move to quantum (on of whom was on VW1 when she was at Leigh Day). It is not clear to me what unique perspective Pete has that between your excellent team, the PG team and the firms on the steer co, cant already be plugged - forgive my ignorance if I am missing something. Suggest we discuss this in more detail on Friday.&nbsp;&nbsp;My application is being considered on an expedited basis - hopefully we will have an idea of timescales asap. I agree this will be a point of focus by the Ds. It is why Alicia is the supervising partner.&nbsp;Unrelated but important, we should discuss the de-designation costs and very low WP offer from the Ds.&nbsp;ThanksAnna&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From:&nbsp;Martyn Day &lt;mday@leighday.co.uk&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Wednesday, October 15, 2025 8:39 AMTo:&nbsp;Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Nichola Marshall &lt;nmarshall@leighday.co.uk&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Sapna Malik &lt;smalik@leighday.co.uk&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Bond turner/Pete/Anna&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;&nbsp;Morning All,&nbsp;Last night I was grabbed by Mal Lewis from Bond turner. Mal is one of the 3-4 CSC lawyers who follows the case very closely. He and his partner, Rachel were very vociferous at the last CSC meeting on the PG issue.&nbsp;He said he remains very concerned about the position of PG following the decision by Cockerill LJ – he felt that the grief from all this is likely to carry on and was worried about the impact on the case longer term.&nbsp;In addition he had seen Pete in the Court today and he asked why we were not using his skills. I explained the sensitivities for PG but he made the point that surely the importance of the case overrode those internal politics. He said he was going to write this week asking for a follow up meeting of the CSC.&nbsp;I am also of the view that we should bring in Pete to the centre of the case to help, as a consultant. Similar to what we do with Ollie Lawson. we could do with him helping the quantum team in particular.&nbsp;Can I also ask again what you are doing re Anna not being certified to work in the Courts. We have Dan Leader here who seemingly is in exactly the same position. He is a barrister who runs the Shell cases for us. We have had to transfer the leadership of the cases to the salaried partner here.&nbsp;I assume the same is true with Anna, ie that one of the other senior members of the team will have to be seen to be the public face of the team. As we know, the Ds will be all over this so we cannot ignore the point. Can I suggest we meet on Friday to discuss.&nbsp;Does 12 work?&nbsp;Martyn&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Martyn&nbsp;Day​​​​Senior Partner020&nbsp;7650&nbsp;1200​leighday.co.ukFollow&nbsp;us&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Panagram, 27 Goswell Road, London, EC1M 7AJ&nbsp;We are committed to protecting your privacy when you use our services and treat all personal data in accordance with our Privacy PolicyDisclaimerThe information contained in this communication from mday@leighday.co.uk sent at 2025-10-15 08:39:49 is confidential and may be legally privileged. It is intended solely for use by those authorised to receive it. If you are not so authorised, you are hereby notified that any disclosure, copying, distribution or taking action in reliance upon the contents of this information is strictly prohibited and may be unlawful. We do not accept service of documents by email.Please note that we only provide our bank account details in a password protected PDF. The password will be communicated separately by telephone. We will never send changes to our bank account details by email outside of this process. If you receive such an email, do not respond to it but contact us separately via your contact at the firm.Visit the Leigh Day website: https://www.leighday.co.ukLeigh Day is a partnership authorised and regulated by the Solicitors Regulation Authority (SRA). The firm's SRA number 