I’ve been in touch with Toremis by email this morning and they have sent the following update. Would you be able to assist with their request please:

I think we have all we need from you/PG on the merits now. We just need to reflect internally on the overall position - this shouldn't take us too long.On the economics - we will review the existing cross-collateralisation arrangements with a view to how they might be adapted for our purposes. We do have two requests on this side
 of things though:


We note that for the existing arrangements, PG is the only claimant-side party. Our current view is that we would also want Gramercy as a party, either in its own right or as a guarantor.
 Is this acceptable to PG/Gramercy?On a related point, we would like to better understand how any settlement proceeds would flow through the existing waterfall(s), including the arrangements with cash flow up to Gramercy.
 Essentially, we would like to be able to understand what the effect of, for example, a settlement with Mercedes, would have on the money flowing through the waterfall in order to assess the extent to which such a settlement would then protect us from adverse
 results against other defendants. It would also be useful to be able to see the effect of varying levels of settlement. We assume that PG has excel models which would allow us to understand this - could we see copies?

Let me know if you need to discuss. I will be available this afternoon.
Kind regards,
