 case. I asked the silks if we could not second your team to work alongside us, but they were clear that would not work. They were clear the Defendants would use the point that Pete G has resigned to say that the funder is exercising undue influence in the
 case and that would apply to the members of your team who are currently within the CRO. The point would become all the more acute as and when it becomes clear that other serios members of the team have resigned. So, we would lose your team and once that happens
 the Defendants will be saying to the Judge that the Claimants do not have the resources to run the trial. We are at a critical junction with huge pressure on the legal teams, an unbelievably heavy workload and preparing for a hugely complex and long trial.
 &nbsp;If we lose the assistance of some of our PG counterparts this is likely to have a catastrophic effect on the litigation to the detriment of all so the point from the Defendants would have a strong reality attached to it.&nbsp;The point will be obvious to the Judge.
&nbsp;
So, the silks were clear that if you look to hold PG’s core legal team to their contracts this runs the serious risk of blowing up the litigation.

&nbsp;
The best route through to safeguard the trial is to allow the team to leave in short order and work elsewhere on the litigation. They can then be re-admitted to the CROs in their new firm. &nbsp;
