 very grateful for your input on the following questions before we share a more advanced draft with you:&nbsp;We understand from previous emails that Craig Shuttleworth is working on the matter. In a similar vein to our letter to Slaughter and May, we can explain that Craig is conducting / leading the proceedings, and you support him. Is that correct? Craig and Celine Barnwell have been involved since the beginning. Craig and I started working on the injunction on 22 February 2025 and then Celine took over - she and I worked together on this from mid-March and she increasingly took the lead as I was meant to move off onto Nox - for example by about late May, I had limited involvement. At the point of the Part 8 claim form which was issued on a protective basis, she was largely leading the matter, partly because there was a fair bit of client facing instructions that were needed and partly because I was meant to start pivoting away from BHP matters from April. &nbsp;Im fairly certain she put in a witness statement on this workstream. The irony is that the decision to initiate this injunction is something Craig and I strongly opposed but Tom G insisted on going ahead.Are there any other partners that are / have been conducting the proceedings that we could mention? The injunction application and supporting witness statement are in Tom Goodhead's name. It was initially envisaged that it would be in Chris Neill's name, for several reasons, including that for the contempt workstream as against BHP, all the witness statements' are by him and he had cost approval and the relationship with the insurers. Of course, both have now gone (Celine I believe is on gardening leave).&nbsp;In terms of the Municipality Applicants’ application for a retrospective extension to the deadline for service of the claim form (supported by Varga 3), who approved the making of the application? (We also assume you did not personally file or serve the application.) it is correct that I did not fil