Thanks for the update Jonathan &nbsp;When do you expect that you will have an indication as to whether there is capacity in the market for the LOI topups ?&nbsp;This is critical &nbsp;From: Jonathan Simon &lt;Jonathan.Simon@wtwco.com&gt; Sent: 23 October 2025 15:40To: Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; James Burke &lt;James.Burke2@wtwco.com&gt;Cc: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Enquiry for Additional ATE Cover – Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Tom&nbsp;I am very sorry to have to report that we cannot provide the ‘top-ups’ via Gemini. This is due to the panel of insurers not being able to cover cases that give rise to a Consumer Duty. Having worked through our matrix on Consumer Duty and tried to get the lead underwriter to change their mind, we have not been able to.&nbsp;James and I are going to contact the wider market now and will report back. Another option would be to utilise Meridian, who could provide policies for all your ‘top-ups’ very quickly, if adequate security can be provided.&nbsp;Kind regardsJonathan&nbsp;Jonathan Simon LLB (Hons)&nbsp;International Head of Litigation and Contingent Risk FINEX GlobalWTWOn behalf of Willis Limited, 51 Lime Street, London, EC3M 7DQ (registered number 181116) On behalf of Willis Towers Watson SA/NV, Quai des Vennes, 4020, Liège, Belgium (registered as a branch in the UK at 51 Lime Street, London, EC3M 7DQ UK Branch Number BR021056) in relation to all EEA-regulated business&nbsp;D: +44 20 3193 9468M: +44 &nbsp;7930 415776&nbsp;jonathan.simon@wtwco.com www.wtwco.com&nbsp;Financial, Professional, and Executive Risks (FINEX)Your Trusted Partner in Managing Complex Risk: Expertly navigating Cyber, Directors &amp; Offic