LINKEDIN POST – 13TH OCT
A defining moment for corporate accountability and environmental justice in the UK. Today, the High Court opens the landmark Dieselgate trial (the Pan NOx PDD), where 1.6 million drivers are seeking justice
 against Mercedes-Benz, Ford, Renault, Nissan, and Peugeot-Citroën.

The claim alleges these carmakers used unlawful “defeat devices” to cheat emissions tests, misleading consumers who believed they were buying cleaner vehicles - while contributing to dangerous levels of air pollution across the UK.

Alicia Alinia, CEO at Pogust Goodhead, said:
“This trial is a mammoth feat by the justice system and goes to the heart of corporate accountability and environmental justice. Drivers were told they were buying cleaner, compliant cars and breathed dirtier air instead. They deserve answers, accountability,
 and compensation.

I want to thank our incredible team and co-counsels for their tireless commitment in bringing this case to court on behalf of hundreds of thousands of drivers
(add @ of the case leads).

Ten years after Dieselgate first came to light, this is a defining moment for affected motorists and for the future of corporate responsibility in the UK.

