 of interference from Gramercy, that we remain as lead Solicitor, we consider that this creates arguably an even bigger need for there to be clear daylight between the case leads and such potential interference. If there is a fear of funder interference, then
 this is even more acute in circumstances where we hold the role of Lead Solicitor, as opposed to that of another Claimant Firm, not&nbsp;least&nbsp;(as we have said before) because we owe duties to all clients, not just those of PG. Can you please give us your / the
 board's opinion on next steps?

