Fergal, Jonathan, &nbsp;I appreciate we are keeping you rather busy today! We turn to the Emissions issue now and more specifically the issues the case leads who have resigned and who are causing trouble (with a view to allowing us to get them to leave immediately, if they are enough of a nuisance). &nbsp;In response to our letter to the D’s lawyers, Mike Burke (one of those who has resigned) has made a number of points in his email relating to SRA guidelines as below . Can you please review asap with a view to supporting with a response please?&nbsp;ThanksR&nbsp;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;&#8203;Raminder&nbsp;GrewalGlobal&nbsp;HR&nbsp;Director+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;718From: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 25 September 2025 17:08To: 'Lawrence, Jonathan' &lt;jonathan.lawrence@clydeco.com&gt;; Fergal Cathie &lt;Fergal.Cathie@clydeco.com&gt;; Trevor Gibson &lt;trevor.gibson@heminsleylaw.com&gt;Cc: Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Signature Application - Action required [CC-UNITEDKINGDOM.145310.10756022]&nbsp;This is the draft notice we had from the D’s.&nbsp;This is against the backdrops that we’ve agreed consensually with the emissions steerco to stand down on a temp basis as co-lead on the merc steerco on the basis of the optical damage caused by Pete Gallagher. We’ve also communicated our intentions to the defendants and confirmed the same to the insurers advising that we’ll be confirming our resourcing plans shortly. &nbsp;​​​​Alicia&nbsp;AliniaChief&nbsp;Executive&nbsp;Officer+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;629From: Lawrence, Jonathan &lt;jonathan.lawrence@clydeco.com&gt; Sent: 25 September 2025 16:51To: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Fergal Cathie &lt;Fergal.Cathie@clydeco.com&gt;; Trevor Gibson &lt;trevor.gibson@heminsleylaw.com&gt;Cc: Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Signature Application - Action required [CC-UNITEDKINGDOM.145310.10756022]&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Alicia&nbsp;So that we can understand the extent of the alleged “misleading position”, and therefore the best response, I should be grateful if you could circulate the letter sent yesterday which named Michael Burke as the PG contact, and Signature’s draft application which he says refers to that fact. Many thanks. &nbsp;Kind regards&nbsp;Jonathan&nbsp;LawrenceLegal&nbsp;Director&nbsp;|&nbsp;Clyde&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Co&nbsp;LLPDirect&nbsp;Dial:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;20&nbsp;7876&nbsp;4307&nbsp;|&nbsp;Mobile:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;7703&nbsp;746&nbsp;321The St Botolph Building | 138 Houndsditch | London EC3A 7AR | UKMain +44 207 876 5000 | Fax +44 333 3000 232&nbsp;| www.clydeco.com&nbsp;​​​​&nbsp;&nbsp;From: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: Thursday, September 25, 2025 4:34 PMTo: Fergal Cathie &lt;fergal.cathie@clydeco.com&gt;; Lawrence, Jonathan &lt;jonathan.lawrence@clydeco.com&gt;; Trevor Gibson &lt;trevor.gibson@heminsleylaw.com&gt;Cc: Raminder Grewal &lt;rgrewal@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: FW: Signature Application - Action required&nbsp;Hi All, &nbsp;We’re having some difficulty with the lawyers currently on their notice period who are trying every which way to get out of their notice periods by quoting various sections of the SRA and pointing to misrep. We’ve managed, successfully, to dampen their efforts based on the Gallagher approach of a repudiatory breach based on the G3 deal and now their efforts are focused on demanding that we tell everyone that they’re in their notice period despite us consistently telling them that any communication needs to be well coordinated and in an effort to preserve the firm and the clients interests. &nbsp;I’d be grateful for your help in drafting a suitable response to all of them as they continue to play these games despite having professional obligations. &nbsp;Many thanksA&nbsp;​​​​Alicia&nbsp;AliniaChief&nbsp;Executive&nbsp;Officer+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;629This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at&nbsp;53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our&nbsp;website.&nbsp;For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our&nbsp;Privacy Policy.From: Alicia Alinia Sent: 25 September 2025 16:29To: Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Emissions Case Leads &lt;EmissionsCaseLeads@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Signature Application - Action required&nbsp;Hi Mike, &nbsp;Thanks for your email. &nbsp;We’ll consider all the points you’ve raised and revert as soon as possible. Anna will be responding on the specific points as they relate to the correspondence from Renault.&nbsp;ThanksA&nbsp;From: Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 25 September 2025 14:24To: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Emissions Case Leads &lt;EmissionsCaseLeads@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Signature Application - Action requiredImportance: High&nbsp;Dear Board,&nbsp;In follow up to my email at 12.52 today, I am writing to ask for immediate attention to be given to addressing my (and the other case leaves) employment position to the Defendants, Court, clients and any other relevant stake holders.&nbsp;As Signature's draft application points out at 8(b)(iii) - a letter was sent out yesterday, naming me as the PG contact.&nbsp;&nbsp;That I am named as the contact appears to have been an administrative oversight, and I put no blame on the sender of the letter, however this has now lead to a misleading position, or what will be a mislead position if not immediately clarified, underpinning the concerns I had regarding paragraph 27 of the letter sent to the Defendants on Tuesday 23 September (see my email at 12.52 today and my suggestion at 15.59 on 23 September).&nbsp;&nbsp;The SRA Code of Conduct at 1.4 says &quot;You do not mislead or attempt to mislead your clients, the court&nbsp;or others, either by your own acts or omissions or allowing or being complicit in the acts or omissions of others (including your client)&quot;&nbsp;By this letter having gone out, and by repeat correspondence continuing to go out in my name on the Ford and Volvo litigations, and the names of the other case leads, without appropriate context that we are working our notice, I have real concerns that the firm is (and I am) in breach of 1.4 of the code of conduct. This applies not only to correspondence to the Defendant firms, but also to clients and any external parties.&nbsp;This requires immediate attention, especially in respect of my position.&nbsp;&nbsp;SL have asked for a response by 4pm. Without wanting to force the hands of the board, I must be insistent that the below (or clarification of that nature) is sent before that deadline to clarify the position:&nbsp;&quot;Pogust Goodhead are considering your application and will respond in due course.&nbsp;&nbsp;As an immediate step, and to address 8(b)(iii) in your application, we confirm categorically that MR Burke does not have conduct of these Pan NOx Litigations. The inclusion of Mr Burke's details in the letter sent to the Defendants on 24 September which named Michael Burke as a &quot;contact&quot;, this was an oversight, and this does not indicate that Mr Burke has conduct of these Pan NOx Litigations on behalf of Pogust Goodhead and Pogust Goodhead's clients. For absolute clarity, Mr Burke does not have conduct of the Pan-NOx Litigations on behalf of Pogust Goodhead.&nbsp;&nbsp;Mr Burke currently has conduct of the Ford NOx Litigation, and the Volvo NOx Litigation, as part of the Pan NOx Litigations. The overall supervision of the Pan-NOx Litigations for Pogust Goodhead will be confirmed in due course as requested in your application.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;We also take this opportunity to advise the Defendants, that Mr Burke has formally tendered his resignation with Pogust Goodhead, as of 15 September 2025, and he is currently working his notice period, the end date which is to be confirmed. Correspondence will be sent directly to the Defendants in those Litigations as soon as possible.&quot;&nbsp;This needs to be sent as soon as possible. I imagine this may be an opportune moment to advise on the other Case Leads and I am happy for this to be incorporated, but the clarity on my position needs to be dealt with immediately.&nbsp;&nbsp;Thanks,&nbsp;Michael&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Michael&nbsp;Burke(He/Him)Partner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7960&nbsp;032&nbsp;34407960&nbsp;032&nbsp;344&nbsp;_____________________________________________________ If our account details change, we will notify these to you by letter, telephone or face-to-face and never by email. Clyde &amp; Co’s privacy notice can be found here Privacy notice: Clyde &amp; Co (clydeco.com) Please could we request that all correspondence with us is sent electronically where possible. For matters subject to the jurisdiction of England &amp; Wales and where you have agreed with the lawyer with the conduct of the case that email service is appropriate, please use this address service@clydeco.com for service, subject to the restrictions set out here . Please copy your email to the lawyer with conduct of the case and include our Clyde &amp; Co reference. This email is sent for and on behalf of Clyde &amp; Co LLP, a limited liability partnership registered in England and Wales under number OC326539 and with its registered office at The St Botolph Building, 138 Houndsditch, London, EC3A 7AR, United Kingdom (Tel: +44 20 7876 5000. Fax: +44 20 7876 5111). Clyde &amp; Co LLP is authorised and regulated by the Solicitors Regulation Authority under number 460690 and uses the word &quot;partner&quot; to refer to a member of the LLP, or an employee or consultant with equivalent standing and qualifications. A list of members is available at: www.clydeco.com. This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you have received this message in error, please notify the sender immediately, destroy this email and any attachments, and do not use, copy, store and/or disclose to any person this email and any attachments. "}

