t;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Fw: Draft email to Claimant Committee/ Lead Solicitor position&nbsp;FYI&nbsp;&nbsp;Sent from Outlook for iOS​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at&nbsp;53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our&nbsp;website.&nbsp;For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our&nbsp;Privacy Policy.From: Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: Monday, September 29, 2025 8:36:07 AMTo: Matt Hunt &lt;mhunt@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Melissa Ferrari &lt;mferrari@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Priyanka Gladson &lt;pgladson@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Matthew Newbould &lt;mnewbould@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Georgina Fallows &lt;gfallows@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Draft email to Claimant Committee/ Lead Solicitor position &nbsp;Thanks Matt. Anna - on the CCom role:&nbsp;I will need to go back and check (the GLO applications were made in 2023) but I think we will have taken instructions on the applications;Unknown - I haven't played a role in Vauxhall.On my cases at least, I provide them with monthly updates. On top of those updates, I will also contact them for instructions on items such as discontinuances or material updates.On the expert applications, I advised them of the applications, but did not take their instructions on the actual content of the application. The key reason for this was due to the confidential nature of the expert reports - the CComs haven't seen the reports yet, becuase they have confidential information and they are not CRO members. They would therefore be unable to advise on what should be kept or removed from the reports.&nbsp;&nbsp;Given the material change to the Litigation that us stepping down as Lead Sols will have, and the change in PGs role (and therefore the CComs roles) in the Litigation, this strikes me as a classic time when we need to a) advise them of why we are doing this and b) take their instructions on doing so.&nbsp;&nbsp;You are right that the relationships with the CComs are less involved than they may be on other Litigations, and that the CComs play a more passive role in the Litigaiton, but we can't just set that to the side. We can't continue to let our clients think we are &quot;running&quot; the Litigation when we are not. I think that risks 1.4 COC.&nbsp;As a bare minimum we need to advise them of a) and long before they hear of it in the press. To actively deny them this information (and to not take instructions) strikes me as a route that we should not consider going down. I suppose we could always run it past counsel (maybe Friston?) to get a seal of approval.&nbsp;There is also a significant cost angle that needs to be considered here in a) the costs that the Ds may seek to recover from us as a result of this application (though I can see the Ds trying to make unjustified hay about it) and b) our foregoing of the ability to recover common costs as Lead Sols (accepting LD can permit us to undertake certain work), and the potential liability of the Cs and their ATE position. This may also have an impact on any CFA deduction we later seek to take as we may no longer have a shortfall on common costs sufficient for the total permitted deduction. Allying this with the recent decision in Mazur&nbsp;(on non-qualified staff doing legal work) - something which we need to think very carefully about in terms of individual work - we may find ourselves in a position where recoverability needs re-assessed. Note - I've already flagged this to Jamie McF and asked him to do a note for us to consider internally how this may impact us. It's very new judgment that everyone is grappling with.&nbsp;&nbsp;The insurers should also be informed of all of this as well though given the Board have been meeting with them, I presume they have kept them up to date with the material changes.&nbsp;&nbsp;Happy to discuss further and to continue to work on the draft to progress it as far as we can (although I think it's pretty much there now and we need Board input to advance it further). Let us know what we can do to help.&nbsp;&nbsp;Thanks,&nbsp;Michael&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Michael&nbsp;Burke(He/Him)Partner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7960&nbsp;032&nbsp;34407960&nbsp;032&nbsp;344From:&nbsp;Matt Hunt &lt;mhunt@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Sunday, September 28, 2025 4:22 PMTo:&nbsp;Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Melissa Ferrari &lt;mferrari@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Priyanka Gladson &lt;pgladson@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Matthew Newbould &lt;mnewbould@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Georgina Fallows &lt;gfallows@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: Draft email to Claimant Committee/ Lead Solicitor position &nbsp;Hi Anna,&nbsp;On the first point, every party has missed almost every single deadline. PCD in particular like to complain about us missing deadlines, but everybody does it (including them) and there are plenty of examples of Ds being late. There are some good quotations from Constable J at the DDH about everybody doing their best and working really hard, and that he isn’t going to accept complaints about deadlines, and Cockerill J has made similar comments at Progress Meetings about all the lawyers working hard and hanging on by their fingernails. As you say, dealing with CROs makes deadlines even harder to meet for the Claimants.&nbsp;Matt​​​​Matt&nbsp;Hunt(He/Him)Legal&nbsp;Director+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;697From:&nbsp;Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Sunday, September 28, 2025 7:50:56 AMTo:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Matt Hunt &lt;mhunt@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Melissa Ferrari &lt;mferrari@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Priyanka Gladson &lt;pgladson@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Matt Hunt &lt;mhunt@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Matthew Newbould &lt;mnewbould@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Georgina Fallows &lt;gfallows@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: Draft email to Claimant Committee/ Lead Solicitor position&nbsp;Morning,&nbsp;I have not had a chance to review yet&nbsp; - there is a lot to get through. The Ds make a big deal about why certain court deadlines were missed in recent weeks regarding openings and experts - from what I have seen this was largely a product of the volume of material, and more relevantly the need to redact confidential information. The openings were filed in court just shy of 4pm (although if someone has the precise time that would help pls). The time consuming piece was applying redactions, awaiting confirmation from Ds about those redactions. Is that broadly correct? I will need more information from the case leads to nail down the specifics.&nbsp;Re lead sols:&nbsp;Grateful if someone could explain to me why we need instructions to step down from Lead Sol - it is not obvious to me why we would need that - we certainly are not obliged to under our engagement letters, CC agreement or LGA and there isnt a regulatory obligation. From discussions with Micheal the working relationship with the CC is arms length. So the nature of the relationship will be determinative of the need to do that.&nbsp;&nbsp;Can I please understand: (1) Did PG get instructions from the CC to sign up for the role of Lead Solicitor in the first place? (2) Was the CC consulted in this regard: e.g. re Vauxhall, did we consult with them then? (3) How often does PG seek instructions from the CC - based on the comms I have seen to date, it seems rather sparce, (4) what sort of issues do we act without seeking instructions from the CC - e.g. re the expert application, did we seek instructions?&nbsp;ThanksAnna&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From:&nbsp;Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Saturday, September 27, 2025 1:19 PMTo:&nbsp;Matt Hunt &lt;mhunt@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Melissa Ferrari &lt;mferrari@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Priyanka Gladson &lt;pgladson@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Matt Hunt &lt;mhunt@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Matthew Newbould &lt;mnewbould@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Georgina Fallows &lt;gfallows@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: Draft email to Claimant Committee/ Lead Solicitor position&nbsp;Thanks for this Matt.&nbsp;I've added this as a SP link here: 2025.09.27 - Draft to Claimant Committees.docx, along with it being attached. I've fleshed it out a bit. The part from &quot;PDD Trial Preparation&quot; is essentially a C&amp;P from the updates I've already sent on Ford and Volvo (including the update on resignation). For Ford and Volvo - it will just be the points re Lead Solicitors that need to be sent.&nbsp;&nbsp;Anna - let us know what we can do to be of assistance. Hopefully this doesn't add to your plate too much (conscious of how much you have got on) and I am happy to get on calls on Monday to work this through and try to get it moving as quickly as possible. Everyone will appreciate this needs to be sent out and we need instructions before we can do anything, so the more we can help to get this moving quicker, the better.&nbsp;&nbsp;Georgie, Pri, Matt N, Melissa, if any of you have any amends, please just make them straight into the link. I've also included Sarah as we may need to consider the cost aspect of this and what advice we need to offer to the CComs. It may be sensible for all of us to have fed into the draft before Anna takes a look.&nbsp;The points re Lead Solicitors i.e. reasoning etc really must come from the Board, not us as case leads. We case leads haven't been privy to any advice / discussions on this so we cannot add it into the draft, nor can we advise the clients&nbsp; (we need to consider if we can send them out, or at least how they're signed off, to the CComs. We'd need to make sure the advice etc is coming from the firm / counsel, and not us case leads. I've inserted appropriate placeholders for the Board to complete.&nbsp;&nbsp;Thanks,​​​​Michael&nbsp;Burke(He/Him)Partner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7960&nbsp;032&nbsp;34407960&nbsp;032&nbsp;344From:&nbsp;Matt Hunt &lt;mhunt@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;26 September 2025 6:06 PMTo:&nbsp;Emissions Case Leads &lt;EmissionsCaseLeads@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Draft email to Claimant Committee/ Lead Solicitor position&nbsp;Hi all,&nbsp;For your review please see the below draft email to Claimant Committees.&nbsp;The &quot;why&quot; obviously needs to be completed by those more in the know; when we agree the template we can send it to them.&nbsp; Anna, for what it is worth, in my experience of the committees I think the more reasons we give, the less likely they are to request a call, and there is some urgency to the email.&nbsp;We have a duty to our clients to send the email, I believe, so this needs to go fairly quickly.&nbsp; In Michael's case it might be more even urgent, since the Defendants know of his resignation: there is a risk that his resignation will go public, and it would be best for the committee relationships if they found out from us.&nbsp;Matt&nbsp;&nbsp;____________________________________________&nbsp;Dear [Case] Claimant Committee,&nbsp;We write with an important update on your case and request for instructions.&nbsp; We should inform you in advance that there is no intention for this to imperil the success of the case.&nbsp;Update&nbsp;First, with regret I have resigned from my position as [X] at Pogust Goodhead.&nbsp; I can confirm that my reasons have nothing to do with the merits of the case: the Claimants' skeleton argument was served on 18 September 2025 and we are confident in its strength.&nbsp; We look forward to holding the Defendants to account, and I will continue to work on the case for as long as I am able.&nbsp;Request for instructions&nbsp;Second, Pogust Goodhead intends to step away from its role as &quot;Lead Solicitor&quot; in the litigation.&nbsp; This is a Court-appointed role that formally entitles the firm to run the case on behalf of all Claimants, not just those who formally instruct this firm.&nbsp; We have done this because [...].&nbsp; Again, this has not been done with any intention to imperil the success of the case or impending trial.&nbsp;Please confirm by return that you agree to instruct Pogust Goodhead to apply to remove itself as Lead Solicitor for this case.&nbsp;If you would like a meeting to discuss the above request for instructions, we are of course happy to arrange a meeting with us and the board of the firm.&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;[X]&nbsp;​​​​Matt&nbsp;Hunt(He/Him)Legal&nbsp;Director+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;697&nbsp;"}

