osed draft to the case leads. Longer than we wish, but they keep bringing up new points. &nbsp;Highlighted points need the blessing of Clydes (yellow) or the agreement of JLG (green).&nbsp;ThanksMatt&nbsp;-----------------------------------------------All,&nbsp;Coming back to you on your email below. First, I want to assure you that we do not intend doing anything, nor have we done anything, that would put us or you in breach of your regulatory or professional &nbsp;requirements. Everything we have done or are intending to do is with the best interests of our clients in mind. Second, regarding your future employment, we expect you to work till the end of your notice period, as contractually agreed. After that period, we understand from the Johnson Law Group that you intend to work there together with Pete Gallagher. We are comfortable for you to do so after the end of your notice period. Johnson Law Group have also confirmed to us that they are not expecting you to join them before the end of the trial. With that in mind, and given your dedication to working in the best interest of the clients, we ask that you work [four] extra days through until the end of the trial, being 19 December 2025. You would be paid your usual salary, and receive all benefits, through until this extended date. If you are agreeable to this arrangement, please could you confirm that to me. Both Pogust Goodhead and Johnson Law Group consider this arrangement will help ensure the clients of Pogust Goodhead (and other firms) are not prejudiced or detrimentally impacted moving forward.Third, it is important to clarify how the Agency Agreement will work – this should give you immediate comfort on the proposed approach.PG’s proposed role is exactly as envisaged in the Pan NOx Agency Agreement, which we have all been working under: PG will, as authorised by the Pan NOx Agency Agreement, act by authorisation of LD with respect to the Common Work delegated to it by LD.&nbsp; The Agency Agreement will enable PG to continue working on the liability trial and quantum workstream while you remain with us working your notice period. In terms of what will change practically, LD will be sole Lead Solicitor, which means that it will be responsible for final decisions in terms of matters such as filing and serving documents, or providing instructions to counsel. PG employees will be delegated work by Leigh Day, in consultation between the two firms, in order to ensure it is able to continue contributing to the cases in the normal course. As you well know, PG and LD have been working together for years, including on behalf of many other solicitor firms, and this proposed updated agreement will authorise PG to continue doing so. You will not be serving two masters – you remain employed by PG, but final decisions as to the conduct of Common Work will be made by Leigh Day. Leigh Day do not and will have any employer-employee relationship with you.&nbsp; As continuing PG employees until the end of your notice period you will be required to continue to work on the Non-Common Work streams as required and directed solely by PG (which includes matters related to the non-Lead Cases, which are not subject to the Agency Agreement). If you have any regulatory concerns that you wish to inform the clients of, please let us know specifically what they are.We, LD and counsel – which has reviewed and signed off on the approach – are comfortable that this is an eminently workable solution which adheres to the existing legal framework and offers the best path forward in the best interests of our clients. We are happy for your to speak to counsel (mindful of the fact that they are also preparing for the PTR and trial). We welcome your input, some of which is being incorporated into the next round of the agency agreement and are obviously happy to deal with any further questions. However, we must make clear that your consent is not needed for us to enter into the agency agreement, as it does 